# TypeScript Conventions

## Types

- Explicit types on exported functions and public APIs; infer locals when obvious
- `interface` for extendable object shapes; `type` for unions/intersections
- Prefer string literal unions over `enum` unless SDE/API IDs require numeric enums
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` + narrowing for external input (ESI, localStorage, shared plan imports)

```typescript
function getErrorMessage(error: unknown): string {
  if (error instanceof Error) return error.message
  return 'Unexpected error'
}
```

## Comments

JSDoc and flow comments: see `code-flow-comments.mdc`.

## React props

Follow `react-component-conventions.mdc`. Named prop interfaces when exported or reused; inline props for small local components.

## Immutability

Return new objects; do not mutate inputs. Zustand actions and plan/user-data updates must spread prior state.

## Errors

- `async/await` + try/catch; narrow `unknown` errors
- User-facing errors: short, actionable copy in sentence case
- Avoid `console.log` in app code; remove debug logs before finishing

## Validation

Validate at trust boundaries:

- Imported/shared plan payloads (`planShare.ts`)
- localStorage user data (`services/sync/types.ts` migrations)
- ESI/API JSON before use

Prefer type guards and explicit checks. This project does not use Zod; do not add it unless requested.

## Secrets

Frontend-only app: no API secrets in source. OAuth client IDs may be public config; never commit refresh tokens or user tokens. Auth storage lives in `services/auth/`.

## Domain logic

Manufacturing math (ME, TE, job time, profit) must match `src/lib/cost.ts` and `eve-industry-domain.mdc`. Do not invent alternate formulas.

## Testing

See `testing-strategy.mdc`. Test hooks and `src/lib/` logic; not component render output.
